      "side": 1,
      "message": "Based on the invariant noted above, I think you could simplify this processing by:\n\n - Changing getAllUniqueRecords to getAllUniqueRecords(List\u003cRecordInfo\u003c?\u003e\u003e)\n - Adding that argument to addNsecRecordsForUniqueNames: `addNsecRecordsForUniqueNames(List\u003cMdnsRecord\u003e destinationList, List\u003cRecordInfo\u003c?\u003e\u003e allRecordsFromService, Iterator\u003cRecordInfo\u003c?\u003e\u003e... answerRecords)`\n - Calling `addNsecRecordsForUniqueNames from addReplyFromService as before, but before adding the address records from the mGeneralRecords list (so before the last loop). For the second \"allRecordsFromService` argument you\u0027d pass in serviceRegistration.allRecords\n - For the address records, call addNsecRecordsForUniqueNames one more time from getReply as you have it now, but `allRecordsFromservice` is `mGeneralRecords` in that case\n\nSo basically: addNsecRecordsForUniqueNames adds nsec records for a ServiceRegistration (excluding general records), or for general records. You call it after adding a reply from a service, or once at the end for the general records. This avoids iterating through all services to build maps of unique records, since as per the invariant, \"unique\" names only appear in a single list (ServiceRegistration or mGeneralRecords)",
      "revId": "f7f5afddc90b74dc95e8fafaaa709477a2ae0673",
